NodalSchureman computes node factors (f) and equilibrium arguments (V0 + u)
for 13 tidal constituents. It is an independent implementation, written from
a written functional specification and from P. Schureman, "Manual of Harmonic
Analysis and Prediction of Tides", U.S. Coast and Geodetic Survey Special
Publication No. 98 (SP98, public domain). No other implementation's source
was used.

It was made in two stages, by two separate parties. A describer read the
earlier webcaltides code, which was derived from libcongen (GPLv3), and wrote
the specification and a 780-point test oracle generated by running that code.
A separate implementer then wrote the module.

The implementer read only the specification, the oracle, three pages of
SP98 (printed pages 154, 162 and 164) and general Ruby documentation. The
implementer also received the coordinator's messages, which gave the tasks and
summarised the changes the reviewers asked for, and contained no code. The
implementer did not read any review of the specification, any reviewer's
report, any webcaltides file or any GPL tide code (libcongen, congen or
XTide). Once, by mistake, the implementer listed the file names in a shared
scratch directory; no file there was opened. The complete record, with the
SHA-256 of each input, is in docs/nodal-cleanroom/PROVENANCE.md.

The functional specification is held by the copyright holder and is available
on request. It is identified by its SHA-256,
4457ec58c3fce39c67971a2351898e2655bb5fbf49cc88dec65f17e5a0b1ad9b, and is not in
this repository by design.
